Fixed #965. When a provider rejects the request (400, 401, 403 or 404), yoyo -p now exits 1, and --output-format json writes a JSON result with "is_error": true. The whole test suite, clippy and fmt pass.

Checked end to end with a local stub server that always answers 404 (dummy key, --no-tools, -p hi):

| mode | before | after |
|---|---|---|
| text | exit 0, 1 byte on stdout | exit 1 |
| --output-format json | exit 0, 1 byte on stdout | exit 1, 350-byte JSON with "is_error":true |

There were two bugs, not one:
1. **The error was shown but never recorded** (`src/prompt.rs`). The last `else` in the `InspectError` handler printed the red `error:` line and set nothing, so the result came back as `Done`. As a result the exit code was 0 and the fallback provider was never tried. That branch now records the error the same way its sibling branches do. The code that later handles it doesn't print it again, and it adds no retry, so stderr looks exactly as before. The fallback provider now runs on these errors, as the issue asked.
2. **`--output-format json never produced JSON, even on success** (src/main.rs`). I only found this after running the stub probe with the first fix in place. That flag only set the output format, while the code that writes JSON only checks the older --json flag. A new small function, wants_json_envelope, now accepts both. text and stream-json are unaffected.

Tests:
• 400/401/403/404 errors are fed through the same steps the real code uses, and the test checks that the exact error text reaches the result the caller gets.
• Cases that must not change stay as they were: a successful turn, the harmless "stream ended" case, context overflow (still triggers auto-compaction), and 503/429 (still retried).
• The JSON-flag function has its own test in main_tests.rs.
• To check the new tests actually catch the bug, I temporarily removed the fix: both new #965 tests failed by name, then passed again once it was restored.

Things I changed that you might not expect:
• **One existing test was flipped, not deleted.** `unrecognised_api_error_surfaces_as_done_not_fatal` pinned the old behaviour on purpose, so that changing it would show up. It is now `..._fatal_not_done`.
• **The work touched 5 files, not the 3 the task listed.** `src/main_tests.rs` is where `main.rs`'s tests live. `tests/module_size.rs` needed `src/prompt.rs`'s size limit raised from 3787 to 3913 lines, and nearly all of that growth is tests. The commit message says so.

The explanation, the before/after numbers and the list of preserved cases are in ARCHITECTURE.md under prompt.rs.
